<%# The allowances, behind a button of their own. They used to live at the
    bottom of the report sheet, under a "Kuota" heading three rows down — the
    readings a reader checks most often were the ones they had to scroll past
    the token breakdown to reach.

    It is a `<details>` rather than a dialog so it needs no script to open. The
    panel hangs above the status row instead of pushing it: the row is at the
    bottom edge of the screen, and a panel below it would open off the page.

    The provider's meters are not drawn with the page: they belong to the
    account, and only the provider knows them, so they cost a request that
    waits until the reader actually opens this. -%>
<details class="usage-sheet usage-sheet-quota"
         hx-get="/s/<%= h(session_id) %>/quota<%= h(token_query) %>"
         hx-target="#usage-quota"
         hx-swap="innerHTML"
         hx-trigger="toggle[this.open]">
  <summary class="usage-toggle" title="<%= h(I18n.t("web.quota.label")) %>" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.quota.label")) %>">
    <%= usage_icon(:quota) %>
  </summary>

  <div class="usage-panel" role="group" aria-label="<%= h(I18n.t("web.quota.label")) %>">
    <div id="usage-quota" class="usage-quota">
      <p class="usage-note"><%= h(I18n.t("web.quota.checking")) %></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
